From: tcmay@netcom.com (Timothy C. May)
Subject: Anachro-, Arachno-, and Anarchocapitalism--A Scorecard

(Since you can't tell the players in the capitalism game without a
scorecard, here's a handy one.)

I enjoyed seeing Michael Morgan's "anachrocapitalism," whether
deliberate or unintentional:

> I asked questions about the ethics of anachrocapitalism. I think the
> burden of proof lays upon the believers of anachrocapitalism.

In addition to the defunct form of capitalism, anachrocapitalism,
there are several other interesting flavors:

* Arachnocapitalism

"Free markets for spiders, scorpions, and mites!" Arachnologists of
the world, unite! My, the Web has many strands.

* Narcocapitalism

The version practiced by the CIA and the Medellin Cartel, with
assistance from the Bloods, Crips, and earnest young narcocapitalists
in the DEA. Marx called narcocapitalism "the opiate of the masses."

* Iraqnocapitalism

BCCI, Banco Nazionale del Lavoro, and Saddam's friends in the CIA. 


* Anarchocapitalism

Not for the anarchophobic, the version favored by Friedman, Vinge, and
many Extropians. Friedman is even a member of the Society for Creative
Anarchism, a group which meets on weekends to bash each other in
tournaments with copies of "Human Action."



-Klaus! von Future Prime

