Date: Thu, 16 Sep 93 19:35:23 PDT
From: tcmay@netcom.com (Timothy C. May)
Subject: META: A suggestion for the list software

Could the list software be twiddled to accept the "::command"
instructions even if they are not the very first line of the message?
The second or third line, for instance?

This came up on Cypherpunks, as Ray of course knows since he's a
valued member of our group there, because the Cypherpunks remailers
have long been using the "::" notation (except we, confusingly, have
to put the "request-remailing-to: foo" command on the following line)
and some folks have a hard time getting the "::" on the first line.

One theory is that some mailers insert an extra line that is not alway
visible.

In any case, allowing more lattitude in the placement of the
"::command" would head off some of the embarassing "accidents" that
have appeared recently.

--Tim May (the other Tim)

